A||||6||zeusrekning||I'm back... :) (DIS question for my 88 coupe)||||1||
Z||000000||zeusrekning||06-04-2001||01:01 PM||||Well i'm back. See there are a lot of new people here. I'm going to replace the windshild in my 88 this month but it still has an electrical problem (i think).At low rpm it seems like i have bad spark or it just i'snt firing right. I know that befor i got it it was driven alot only on 3 cylinders. I'm wondering if i can take the doodads (two things that act as the distributor) of my 87 coupe and put them on my 88?? I think that is my problem , but i didn't know if anything was changed from 87 to 88. also .. does anyone have any good info on door glass replacement, and door panel replacement?Thanks in advance.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-04-2001||01:39 PM||||First thing is check plugs and wires. make sure plugs are gapped to 0.060.<P>Next check MAP sensor and vac lines carefully. Problems with MAP will screw up ignition operation.<P>The ignition for all DIS 2.5l is the same. Bunches of notes in my cave about DIS motors.<P>There are notes on the doors and door glass in my cave that may help...||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||06-04-2001||03:28 PM||||thanks, I'll check into it after i post this. What is the map sensor?? manifold air pressure? where is it? Is it easier to replace the whole door and put my old door skins on the new donar door? thank you.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||06-04-2001||10:31 PM||||The MAP sensor (Manifold Absolute Pressure), is located on the air cleaner housing.  It is a black box with an electrical connector, and also a vacuum line that runs to the base of the TBI.  Check that line for cracks, especially check to see if the rubber elbows are cracked/rotten.<P>As for the door glass, I had Autoglass Specialists come out and replace mine for about $140.  After I watched the guy do it, I realized that it isnt that hard at all.  All you need to do is pull the inner door skin, remove the water deflector paper, raise the glass until you can get at the rivets, and drill away.  You will have to reposition the glass everyone once and a while to get at different rivets.  If you dont have the correct tool to set the new rivets, you could probably use nuts, bolts, and washers to hold the glass in the track...make sure to use nylock nuts and loctite if you do.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||06-05-2001||03:13 AM||||I can use carb cleaner to check for cracks in vacume lines right???<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||06-05-2001||10:04 AM||||Yes you can, carb cleaner should make the car sputter or die.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||06-05-2001||10:53 AM||||I had that happen to my 88coupe. It had new Wires and still acted up. It needed Low resistence plug wires. I got some nice accel 8mm and it ran great.<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
